---
/**
 * PRIVACY POLICY — /privacy/
 * Business details (email, address, registration number) come from
 * src/config/site.ts. When you change this policy, update
 * LEGAL.policiesLastUpdated in that file.
 */
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT, LEGAL, SITE } from '../config/site';
const mail = `mailto:${CONTACT.email}`;
---
<PolicyLayout title="Privacy Policy" path="/privacy/" description="How The Standard Solutions collects, uses and protects personal information when you use our website and services.">
  <p>This policy explains how {LEGAL.tradingName} ("we", "us", "our") collects, uses and protects personal information when you visit <a href="/">{SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>, contact us or use our services.</p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>{LEGAL.tradingName} is a {LEGAL.entityType} (registration number {LEGAL.registrationNumber}) providing accounting, bookkeeping and business-formation support services.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Address:</strong> {LEGAL.fullAddress}</li>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={mail}>{CONTACT.email}</a></li>
    <li><strong>WhatsApp / phone:</strong> {CONTACT.phoneDisplay}</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We are responsible for deciding how your personal information is used (the "controller").</p>

  <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>When you contact us</h3>
  <p>If you book a consultation, complete our enquiry form, message us on WhatsApp or email us, we receive the details you choose to share — typically your name, email address, phone number, company name, country and a description of what you need.</p>
  <h3>When you become a client</h3>
  <p>To deliver our services we may collect identity and verification documents (for example passports and proof of address for directors, shareholders and owners), company information, financial records, bank statements, invoices, payroll data and access to your accounting software.</p>
  <h3>When you browse the website</h3>
  <p>Our website does not use cookies, advertising trackers or analytics tools. Our hosting provider, Cloudflare, automatically processes limited technical data (such as IP address, browser type and the pages requested) to deliver the website securely and protect it from attacks.</p>

  <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to enquiries and arrange consultations.</li>
    <li>To prepare proposals and deliver the services you engage us for.</li>
    <li>To carry out identity checks required by formation partners, registries and service providers.</li>
    <li>To send invoices and manage payments.</li>
    <li>To meet our legal, regulatory and record-keeping obligations.</li>
    <li>To keep our website and systems secure.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for advertising.</p>

  <h2>4. Our legal basis</h2>
  <p>Where data-protection laws such as the UK GDPR apply, we rely on: <strong>contract</strong> (to provide services you request), <strong>legal obligation</strong> (for example record-keeping and identity checks), <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (for example responding to enquiries and keeping our website secure) and, where required, <strong>consent</strong>, which you can withdraw at any time.</p>

  <h2>5. Who we share information with</h2>
  <p>We share personal information only where needed to provide our services, for example with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Authorised company formation partners and registered-agent partners.</li>
    <li>Government bodies and registries, such as Companies House, HMRC, US state filing offices, the IRS, SECP and FBR, when filing on your instructions.</li>
    <li>Software and communication providers we use to run the business, such as Google (Calendar, Forms, Gmail), WhatsApp (Meta), Cloudflare and cloud accounting platforms (Xero, QuickBooks, Zoho).</li>
    <li>Professional advisers, or authorities where we are required by law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These providers have their own privacy policies, which we encourage you to read.</p>

  <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
  <p>We are based in Pakistan and work with clients and providers in other countries, so your information may be processed outside your home country. Where we transfer personal information, we use reputable providers with appropriate safeguards and share only what is necessary.</p>

  <h2>7. How long we keep information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Enquiries that do not lead to an engagement:</strong> up to 24 months.</li>
    <li><strong>Client records:</strong> for the duration of the engagement and up to 6 years afterwards, or longer if the law requires.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. How we protect information</h2>
  <p>We use access controls, two-factor authentication, encrypted connections and reputable cloud providers to protect information. Access is limited to people who need it to deliver our services. Please do not send sensitive documents through our enquiry form — we will provide a secure method once we begin working together.</p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct or delete your personal information, restrict or object to its use, receive a copy in a portable format and withdraw consent. To make a request, email <a href={mail}>{CONTACT.email}</a>. We will respond within one month.</p>
  <p>If you are in the UK and are unhappy with how we have handled your information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at ico.org.uk. We would appreciate the chance to resolve your concern first.</p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>Our services are intended for businesses and adults. We do not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The "last updated" date at the top shows when it was last changed.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy? Email <a href={mail}>{CONTACT.email}</a> or write to us at {LEGAL.fullAddress}.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
